1.3.2 Hyperbolic Metrics
Having introduced some basics of hyperbolic geometry, we now discuss the connections between tree
metrics and hyperbolic spaces and motivate the use of hyperbolic spaces to represent hierarchical
data.
Before its use in ML, hyperbolic geometry has been extensively studied to understand the
geometry of complex networks and theoretical studies showed that many real-world networks exhibit
hierarchical and tree-like structures with underlying hyperbolic geometry [108, 139]. But how can we
identify these hierarchical and tree-like structures? This can be formalized the notion of Gromov
delta-hyperbolicity [3, 49, 78] which we discuss next.


