hyperbolic GRL methods [136, 150], HGCN leverages node features making it inductive and
applicable to unseen test data. Our experiments show that our method leads to significant im
provements in terms of expressiveness and performance compared to Euclidean analogs on graphs
which exhibit different extents of hierarchical structure. On the semi-supervised node classification
